Z||000000||BAM-BAM||06-26-2001||12:20 AM||||    Ok, I successfully removed my door carpet (wasn't to hard) and now I'm ready to install the new carpet. What I have is 1 yrd of extra carpet from when I ordered my carpet from ACC. I know someone has had to have done this, so if you could give me any tips on how to lay it out, I would greatly appriciate it. Or, I could use my old carpet as a template. <BR>   Also, for those who question how to remove it. I just started pealing it back and using a razor at the edge where it pulls up. Took me about 20 minutes per side. It looks as though they used a type of rubber cement, spead on both surfaces then stuck together. Wasn't hard at all, save the blister on my finger from the razor blade. TIA.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||6
Z||000001||sjp777||06-26-2001||12:26 AM||||I did mine in black leather. Just lay it on there and trim around. Leave about 2 inches on the sides and bottom to wrap around. The top you'll have to cut exact to match the curve around where the arm rests go.<P>3M spray adhesive works good on the flat, then I used hot glue on the back for the wrapped edges.<P>Getting the old off was the hardest part.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
